    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"repeat\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f501\" role=\"img\" title=\"repeat\">:repeat:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14966#pullrequestreview-5633827813\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 634504357,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792786144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14966#discussion_r4363772825\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't think that it is worthwhile for us to track whether check_write has issued the permit, we just need to trap when write exceeds the permitted size, which it already does. So, all of these changes to the cli streams should be thrown away - they already obey the spec from my reading as well as what we enforce in other streams.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634504359,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792786144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14966#discussion_r4363751989\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>this const should be hoisted out to the parent scope, and used in the check_write method as well</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634504361,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792786144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>pchickey <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14966#issuecomment-6373772508\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14966\">PR #14966</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This PR is borderline on my radar of needing more careful human review before submission - the changes to c-api and pipe are fundamentally completely different to those proposed in the changes to the stdout/stderr streams, and it would have been nice if you had caught that before submitting.</p>\n</blockquote>",
